  "prefLabel": "Res 102.01 Department",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Res 102.01 Department. The department of resources and economic development is under the executive direction of the commissioner, and consists of a division of forests and lands, a division of parks and recreation, a division of travel and tourism development, and a division of economic development. The descriptions of the divisions that follow below are not exhaustive and simply describe the main purpose and scope of each.\n\nSource. #2221, eff 12-23-82; ss by #2979, eff 2-21-85; EXPIRED 2-21-91\n\nNew. #5798, eff 3-18-94, EXPIRED: 3-18-00\n\nNew. #7395, eff 11-1-00, EXPIRED: 7-1-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/res100.html"
